# Signing in with an external provider

If your Herold deployment is connected to an external sign-in provider
(for example Pocket ID), you can sign in to the web interface through it
instead of typing your password. Your password keeps working, and mail
apps (IMAP/SMTP) continue to use your password or app passwords.

## Link your account

Before the provider can sign you in, link it to your Herold account once:

1. Sign in with your email address and password.
2. Open *Settings > Security*. The section *Sign-in providers* lists the
   providers your administrator has set up.
3. Click *Link* next to the provider. Your browser goes to the provider;
   sign in there and approve the request.
4. You return to *Settings > Security* with the message "Your account is
   now linked", and the provider shows *Linked as* followed by the account
   you used there.

The link is to that particular account at the provider, not to an email
address: the provider account's email does not have to match your Herold
address.

## Sign in

On the sign-in page, click *Sign in with* followed by the provider's name.
After you sign in at the provider you are taken straight to your mail.

If the sign-in page reports that the provider account is not linked to a
Herold account, sign in with your password and link it as described above.
If it reports that the sign-in was started in a different browser or tab,
start it again from the sign-in page in the browser you are using.

## Unlink

In *Settings > Security*, click *Unlink* next to the provider and confirm.
The provider can then no longer sign you in. Signing out of Herold does not
sign you out of the provider.
